      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Belgrade was officially platted by the Pacific Land Company in 1887 and became a village on March 19, 1888.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/belgrade_minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1988, the town unveiled the world’s tallest crow statue—a 40‑foot metal bird—celebrating its centennial.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
